      <p>These sites preserve places where enslaved people were held in bondage and forced to labor, and a thoughtful visitor plans the day with that history in mind rather than treating it purely as a scenic outing. Whitney Plantation in particular was created explicitly to center that history rather than soften it, and visitors who want the fullest, most historically honest picture of River Road's past are well served by including it in their day.</p>
